'' A 'ustring * N' AS A PRINT ITEM is copied into a ustring temporary for fb_PrintUStr, and a
'' LITERAL assigned to one is read from its source, escapes and all. 'print u' printed
'' nothing, and '!"a<e-acute><CJK>b"' held its UTF-8 bytes. See PrintOne in mir/lowerio.bas
'' and LowerZstrAssignTo in mir/lowersub.bas.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/fixed-ustring-print.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl void fb_PrintUStr(0, @$tmp
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl void fb_UStrDelete(@$tmp
'' EXPECT-OUT: "a\u00E9\u4E2Db"
'' EXPECT-OUT: "x\u0009\u00E9"
'' EXPECT-NOT: \u00C3\u00A9
